, "watch": "Any late-breaking polling showing a tighter race, or a major shift in the national House environment, could move this toward Likely D.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Eugene Vindman (D) is running."]}, "overview": "First-term incumbent Eugene Vindman defends a Northern Virginia–area seat with a modest Democratic lean against Republican Doug Ollivant, a former national security official who won the GOP primary in August. Vindman has raised over $12 million and holds more than $6.5 million on hand, dwarfing Ollivant's roughly $250,000 war chest, giving the incumbent an overwhelming advertising and organization advantage.\n\nEvery major race rater places the district at Likely D or better, and prediction markets price Vindman's chances around 94-95%. Ollivant announced a blood cancer diagnosis in early October but says he will stay in the race. With no public general-election polling available, the forecast rests on fundamentals, ratings, and markets, all pointing to a comfortable Vindman win.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.972, "margin": 13.04}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9562, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9664, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9585, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9406, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9612, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9637, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9667, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9827, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9791, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9746, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9559, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9685, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9681, "margin": 13.0}]}